_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_

**Handle clipboard write errors.**

`navigator.clipboard.writeText()` returns a Promise that can reject (e.g., permissions denied, non-secure context). Currently, the success toast shows regardless of whether the copy actually succeeded.


<details>
<summary>🛡️ Proposed fix to handle clipboard errors</summary>

```diff
-  const copyToClipboard = () => {
-    navigator.clipboard.writeText(feedUrl);
-    setHasCopied(true);
-    toast({
-      title: 'Copied!',
-      description: 'Feed URL copied to clipboard',
-    });
-    setTimeout(() => setHasCopied(false), 2000);
+  const copyToClipboard = async () => {
+    try {
+      await navigator.clipboard.writeText(feedUrl);
+      setHasCopied(true);
+      toast({
+        title: 'Copied!',
+        description: 'Feed URL copied to clipboard',
+      });
+      setTimeout(() => setHasCopied(false), 2000);
+    } catch {
+      toast({
+        title: 'Copy failed',
+        description: 'Could not copy to clipboard',
+        variant: 'destructive',
+      });
+    }
   };
```
</details>

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
In `@apps/web/src/components/dashboard/integrations/feed-url-section.tsx` around
lines 56 - 64, The copyToClipboard function currently calls
navigator.clipboard.writeText(feedUrl) without handling rejection, so it always
shows the success toast; update copyToClipboard to await or chain the Promise
from navigator.clipboard.writeText(feedUrl) and handle errors: on success call
setHasCopied(true) and show the success toast, schedule setHasCopied(false) as
before; on failure do not set hasCopied, instead show an error toast (e.g.,
title "Copy failed" with error.message) and optionally console.error the error.
Keep references to copyToClipboard, navigator.clipboard.writeText, setHasCopied,
and toast when making these changes.
```

</details>

